25:     """
26:     Fill unobstructed horizontal gaps between neighboring foreground objects with maroon.
27: 
28:     Input structure
29:     - The grid has one connected background color and one foreground color split into several 4-connected solid rectangles.
30:     - Foreground rectangles can be horizontally separated while overlapping in their row spans.
31:     Rule
32:     - For every pair of foreground rectangles with separated column spans and overlapping row spans, consider the rectangle between their bounding boxes.
33:     - Paint that between-box region maroon when no third foreground rectangle has a bounding box crossing both that horizontal gap and the same shared row span.
34:     - Keep all original pixels unchanged.
